      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "> **Test fixture.** This board points at `imagery.test`, a host that does not resolve. It exists so the end-to-end suite can intercept its requests; opened by hand the map stays empty, and that is correct.\n\n# One service, many years\n\nThree years of an **invented** service. Like its siblings `zarr` and `cogPainted`, this board points at a host that does not exist (`imagery.test`): it exists so the end-to-end suite can intercept its requests, so **opened by hand the map stays empty, and that is correct**.\n\nWhat it pins down is that the mosaic rule — the one that picks the year — is set by the map's clock, without rebuilding the layer.\n\nTo see it working for real, against Impact Observatory's actual service, `esri-image` and `esri-identify` are on the sources bench (`:3002`)."
      }
    },
